## 3.1 Shared code rules

- `VsBadge`, `TabPageShell` and `AppCarImage` are shared. Do not copy them into the Compare folder.
- `CompareCatalogue` is the single data entry point for the feature. Widgets must not build their own lists of cars or reviews.
- The `Car` model lives in `filter_results.dart`. Import it from there. Do not create `new_cars.dart` (see section 22, P0-2).

# 4. SCREEN FLOW AND NAVIGATION MAP

```
Bottom navigation (index 2, "Compare")
        |
        v
CompareScreen  (lib/features/bottom/compare/compare.dart)
  |--- top bar "Search"  ----------------> AppRoutes.searchCars  -> CarSearchScreen
  |--- top bar "Saved reviews" -----------> SavedReviewsScreen
  |
  |--- tap an empty / filled selector ---> SelectCarScreen  --(returns Car)--> back to CompareScreen
  |--- "+ Add Car" ------------------------> SelectCarScreen (first free slot)
  |--- "Compare" (both slots filled) -----> CompareDetailsScreen(carA, carB)
  |--- tap a popular comparison card -----> CompareDetailsScreen(pair.a, pair.b)
  |--- tap a review card / "Read More" --> ExpertReviewScreen(review)
  |       |--- "View Full Comparison" ----> CompareDetailsScreen(review.carA, review.carB)
  |       |--- bookmark -----------------> CompareCatalogue.toggleSaved(review.id)
  |       |--- share ---------------------> Clipboard
  |--- "Read all expert reviews" ---------> AllReviewsScreen
  |           |--- tap a review ----------> ExpertReviewScreen(review)
```

Rules:

- Tab switching must not push routes. The shell animates the `PageView`.
- Sub-screens are pushed with `MaterialPageRoute` and popped with `Navigator.pop`.
- `CompareDetailsScreen` is always reached with two concrete `Car` objects. Never push it with null cars.
- `SelectCarScreen` returns the selected `Car` through `Navigator.pop(car)`. The caller must handle a null result (user pressed back).

# 5. COMPLETE PAGE STRUCTURE

The Compare tab is a single vertical scroll (`ListView`, `BouncingScrollPhysics`) with these blocks in this exact order:

1. Top bar (`TabPageShell`) — title "Compare Cars", search action, saved reviews action.
2. Two car selector panels side by side with a centred "VS" badge.
3. Action row — "+ Add Car" (outlined) and "Compare" (filled teal).
4. Section heading "POPULAR CAR COMPARISONS".
5. Popular comparison cards (2 visible initially).
6. "Less Comparisons" / "More Comparisons" buttons.
7. Section heading "COMPARISON TESTS".
8. Horizontally scrollable expert review carousel.
9. Full-width "Read all expert reviews" outlined button.

Do not split these blocks into separate screens. The page is one scrollable surface inside the tab.

# 6. GLOBAL VISUAL DESIGN

## 6.1 Colors

### Professional Color System for Ethiopian Car Sales Application

This documentation defines a complete color system for a modern, professional Ethiopian car sales application with **Muted Blue** as the primary brand color.

#### Primary Brand Color

| Color | Hex | Purpose |
|-------|-----|---------|
| **Muted Blue** | `#647FA3` | Brand identity, selected navigation icons, active states, important highlights |
| **Dark Muted Blue** | `#526D91` | Primary buttons, important actions |
| **Light Blue** | `#EAF0F7` | Selected filter chips, subtle highlights |
| **Deep Navy** | `#34465E` | Headings, important text, strong visual emphasis |

#### Supporting Colors

| Color | Hex | Purpose |
|-------|-----|---------|
| **White** | `#FFFFFF` | Scaffold background, card backgrounds |
| **Cool Gray** | `#F1F4F8` | Secondary surfaces, input backgrounds |
| **Secondary Text Gray** | `#64748B` | Section headings, metadata, spec labels |
| **Border Gray** | `#D9E0E8` | Card borders, dividers, input outlines |

#### Color Usage Rules (for Compare Feature)

- Use white (`#FFFFFF`) as the scaffold background
- Use muted blue (`#647FA3`) for selected states, active chips, accent elements
- Use darker blue (`#526D91`) for primary actions and filled buttons
- Use light blue (`#EAF0F7`) for selected filter chips and subtle highlights
- Use deep navy (`#34465E`) for section headings and important text
- Use cool gray (`#F1F4F8`) for secondary surfaces and card backgrounds
- Use border gray (`#D9E0E8`) for dividers, card borders, input outlines
- Keep comparisons visually distinct without excessive colors
- Use **green** (`#16A34A`) for successful action states
- Use **red** (`#DC2626`) for error states or destructive actions
- Use **orange** (`#F97316`) only for relevant warnings

#### Existing Color Tokens (Preserved - AppColors class)

| Token | Hex | Usage in Compare |
| ----- | ----- | ---------------- |
| `AppColors.background` | `#FFFFFF` | Scaffold background |
| `AppColors.surface` | `#FAFAFA` | Cards, panels, chips (update to cool gray variant) |
| `AppColors.divider` | `#E0E0E0` | 1px card borders, dividers, skeleton blocks |
| `AppColors.textPrimary` | `#1A1A2E` | Car names, titles, spec values |
| `AppColors.textSecondary` | `#6B6B6B` | Section headings, metadata, spec labels |
| `AppColors.textDisabled` | `#BDBDBD` | Empty/error icon placeholders |
| `AppColors.teal` | `#0F8F83` | Primary accent: preserved for VS badge, chip selection |
| `Color(0xFFEAF4F3)` | pale teal | Empty selector icon circle (keep existing) |

#### Color Implementation in Flutter

All colors should reference `AppColors` constants from `lib/core/constants/app_colors.dart`. The Compare feature should use the centralized color system while maintaining its existing visual structure.

**Example Usage:**

```dart
// Scaffold background
body: Container(color: AppColors.background), // #FFFFFF

// Card fill
child: Container(color: AppColors.surface), // #FAFAFA (update to cool gray variant)

// Dividers and borders
child: Container(decoration: BoxDecoration(border: Border.all(color: AppColors.divider)))

// Text colors
Text(
  style: TextStyle(
    color: AppColors.textPrimary, // #1A1A2E
  ),
  text: 'BMW 7 Series vs Mercedes-Benz',
)

// Spec labels
Text(
  style: TextStyle(
    color: AppColors.textSecondary, // #6B6B6B
  ),
  text: 'Price',
)

// Button styles - using new brand colors
ElevatedButton(
  onPressed: () {},
  style: ElevatedButton.styleFrom(
    backgroundColor: AppColors.brandPrimaryDark, // #526D91 for primary
    foregroundColor: Colors.white,
  ),
)

// Outlined button with muted blue
OutlinedButton(
  onPressed: () {},
  style: OutlinedButton.styleFrom(
    side: BorderSide(color: AppColors.brandPrimary), // #647FA3 for muted blue
    foregroundColor: AppColors.brandPrimary,
  ),
)

// Light blue for selected state
Container(
  color: AppColors.brandPrimaryLight, // #EAF0F7 for selected filter
)

# 7. TOP BAR AND HEADER ACTIONS

The Compare page uses `TabPageShell` so it keeps the app-wide header treatment and the bottom navigation supplied by `NavigationShell`.

```dart
TabPageShell(
  title: 'Compare Cars',
  trailing: [
    _CompareTopAction(icon: AppIcons.search, tooltip: 'Search', onTap: ...),
    const SizedBox(width: AppDimens.sm),
    _CompareTopAction(icon: AppIcons.bookmarkBorder, tooltip: 'Saved reviews', onTap: ...),
  ],
  child: const _CompareBody(),
)
```

- `_CompareTopAction` is a 42x42 rounded square with `AppColors.surface` fill, 1px `AppColors.divider` border, 21px icon in `AppColors.textSecondary`, wrapped in a `Tooltip`.
- Search pushes the named route `AppRoutes.searchCars` (`/search-cars` -> `CarSearchScreen`).
- Saved reviews push `SavedReviewsScreen` with `MaterialPageRoute`.
- `TabPageShell` renders a `Column` (not `Expanded`) so it works inside the shell's `PageView`; the child must be a scrollable widget.

# 8. CAR SELECTOR

Two `_CarSelectorPanel` widgets sit in a `Row` of two `Expanded` children inside a `Stack` with `alignment: Alignment.center`. The `VsBadge` is the centered overlay on the seam.

## 8.1 Empty panel (`_EmptyPanel`)

- Fixed height 280.
- Pale teal circle, 92x92, radius 46, colour `#EAF4F3`.
- `Icons.directions_car_filled`, size 46, colour `AppColors.teal`.
- Label "Select Car" in `titleSmall`, primary colour.
- Tapping anywhere on the panel opens `SelectCarScreen` for that slot.

## 8.2 Selected panel (`_SelectedPanel`)

- Fixed height 280, `AppColors.surface`, `radiusLg`, 1px divider border, clipped.
- `AppCarImage(asset: car.image, height: 160)`.
- Below the image, padded by `AppDimens.md`: car name (`titleSmall`, 1 line, ellipsis), year (`bodySmall`, secondary, `-` when missing), price (`labelLarge`, teal).
- A circular remove button sits at the top right (6px inset, `AppColors.surface` fill, elevation 1, `Icons.close` size 18). Tapping it clears that slot and rebuilds the page.

## 8.3 Selection rules

- The picker result is assigned to the slot that was tapped.
- "+ Add Car" fills the first free slot: slot A when A is empty, otherwise slot B.
- When both slots are filled, "+ Add Car" must not silently fail. Either hide/disable it or replace the current selection (see section 22, P1-3).
- Slot state lives in `_CompareBodyState` as `Car? _carA` and `Car? _carB`.

# 9. PRIMARY ACTIONS

| Button | Style | Enabled when | Result |
| ------ | ----- | ------------ | ------ |
| "+ Add Car" | `OutlinedButton`, teal text, teal border, `radiusMd`, vertical padding 14 | At least one slot free | Opens `SelectCarScreen` |
| "Compare" | `FilledButton`, teal background, `radiusMd`, vertical padding 14 | Both slots filled | Pushes `CompareDetailsScreen(carA, carB)` |

Both buttons are `Expanded` inside one `Row` separated by `AppDimens.md`, so they always have equal width.

The "Compare" button uses `onPressed: null` when the comparison is not possible. This is the only disabled state; do not hide the button.

# 10. POPULAR CAR COMPARISONS SECTION

## 10.1 Data

`CompareCatalogue.fetchPopularPairs()` returns `List<({Car a, Car b})>`.

The pairs are generated from the shared `newCars` catalogue by combining every distinct car with every later car, so the same combination never appears twice:

```dart
for (var i = 0; i < newCars.length; i++) {
  for (var j = i + 1; j < newCars.length; j++) {
    pairs.add((a: newCars[i], b: newCars[j]));
  }
}
```

With the current four-car catalogue this yields six pairs. The list grows automatically when the catalogue grows, so no hardcoded pair list is allowed.

## 10.2 Card (`_PopularCompareCard`)

- Full-width card, `AppDimens.md` padding, `AppDimens.sm` bottom margin, `radiusLg`, surface fill, 1px divider border.
- Image row: two `Expanded` `AppCarImage` blocks at height 96 with `radiusMd` and icon size 24, with a centred `VsBadge` on the seam.
- Name row: two `Expanded` text blocks showing `'<brand> <modelName>'`, `titleSmall`, max 2 lines, ellipsis.
- Price row: two `Expanded` text blocks showing `priceText`, `labelLarge`, teal, max 1 line, ellipsis.
- The whole card is one `InkWell` that opens `CompareDetailsScreen(pair.a, pair.b)`.

## 10.3 Paging

- `_initialPairs = 2` cards are shown initially.
- "More Comparisons" reveals two more cards (`_visiblePairs += 2`).
- "Less Comparisons" resets back to 2 and is only shown when more than 2 are visible.
- Both buttons are outlined teal, equal width, separated by `AppDimens.md`.

