## 11.2 "Read all expert reviews"

A full-width outlined teal button below the carousel that pushes `AllReviewsScreen`.

# 12. SELECT CAR SCREEN

Opened by tapping a selector panel or "+ Add Car". Full-screen `Scaffold` with `AppColors.background`.

## 12.1 App bar search field

- The `AppBar` has no back button and `titleSpacing: 0`; the title itself is the search field container (height 44, surface fill, `radiusMd`, divider border).
- `TextField` with `autofocus: true`, hint "Search make, model or year", prefix search icon size 22, suffix clear button when the query is not empty.
- `TextEditingController` is disposed in `dispose()`.

## 12.2 Filters

Two filter rows, both horizontal chip lists of height 36 with `BouncingScrollPhysics`:

1. "Brand" — distinct brands of the catalogue, sorted ascending.
2. "Year" — distinct years parsed from the car name, sorted descending.

Chips are `ChoiceChip` with `showCheckmark: false`, `radius 26`, surface background, divider border, teal when selected. Tapping the selected chip clears the filter.

## 12.3 Results

- `_results` filters the catalogue by keyword (matches `name` or `brand`, case-insensitive), then by brand, then by year.
- Each `_CarOptionRow` shows a 64x48 image, `'<brand> <modelName>'`, `'<year> · <fuel> · <transmission>'`, the teal price and a chevron.
- Tapping a row pops the screen with that `Car`.
- Empty state text: "No cars match your search", centered with `AppDimens.xxl` top padding.

# 13. COMPARE DETAILS SCREEN

`CompareDetailsScreen(carA:, carB:)` — the core output of the feature.

## 13.1 App bar

- Title "Compare" (`titleMedium`).
- Leading back arrow that pops the screen.
- One action: share (`AppIcons.share`, secondary colour) with tooltip "Share comparison".

## 13.2 Header row

Two `_ComparisonHeader` widgets in a `Row` of two `Expanded`, with a `VsBadge(size: 40)` centred on the seam.

Each header shows:

1. Label "Car 1" / "Car 2" (`labelSmall`, letterSpacing 1.1).
2. Image, height 120, `radiusMd`, `BoxFit.cover`, error fallback icon.
3. `'<brand> <modelName>'`, 1 line, ellipsis.
4. Year (`-` when missing).
5. Teal price.

## 13.3 Actions

- "Swap Cars" — outlined teal with `Icons.swap_horiz`. Swaps the two cars in state, so every row flips.
- "Reset" — outlined secondary with `Icons.refresh`. Today it simply pops the screen (see section 22, P1-4).

## 13.4 Specification sections

Sections are rendered by `_ComparisonSection` as a surface card with a title row, a 1px divider, then one row per specification: a 110 wide label, then two `Expanded` value columns.

| Section | Rows | Source |
| ------- | ---- | ------ |
| Basic Information | Price, Year, Condition, Mileage | `priceText`, `year`, hard-coded "Used", `km` |
| Engine & Performance | Engine size, Engine type, Power, Torque, Cylinders | `N/A` (not in the model) |
| Transmission | Transmission, Drive type | `transmission`, `N/A` |
| Fuel | Fuel type, Fuel economy | `fuel`, `N/A` |
| Dimensions | Length, Width, Height, Ground clearance, Boot space | `N/A` |
| Features | Air conditioning, Airbags, ABS, Reverse camera, Parking sensors, Sunroof, Apple CarPlay, Android Auto, Other features | `N/A` |

Rules:

- A missing or blank value renders `N/A`. Never substitute a guess.
- The label column is fixed at 110 wide; values are `Expanded` so long text wraps.
- Rows use `crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.start` so wrapped values do not clip.

